{% comment %}
Hacker News - Full Layout
Mirrors TRMNL's native Hacker News plugin, plus a QR code to
trmnl.tomrad.se/las/hn where the same numbers link to each story.
Columns are split here rather than by the overflow engine so the QR rail fits.
{% endcomment %}

<style>
  .hn { display: grid; gap: 0 24px; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr) auto; height: 100%; width: 100%; }
  .hn__col { display: grid; grid-template-rows: repeat(8, minmax(0, 1fr)); min-height: 0; min-width: 0; }
  .hn__col .item { align-items: center; min-height: 0; overflow: hidden; }
  .hn__col .title { -webkit-box-orient: vertical; -webkit-line-clamp: 1; display: -webkit-box; overflow: hidden; }
  .hn__x { display: none; }
  .hn__read { align-items: center; align-self: end; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .hn__read svg { display: block; height: 87px; width: 87px; }
  .hn__read .label { margin-top: 4px; }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .hn__og { display: none; }
    .hn__x { display: grid; grid-template-rows: repeat(12, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .hn__col .title { -webkit-line-clamp: 2; }
    .hn__read svg { height: 116px; width: 116px; }
  }
</style>

